---
// Cloudflare Web Analytics beacon (BUILD_PLAN M1 item 4, D-029, D-031). Renders NOTHING unless PUBLIC_CF_ANALYTICS_TOKEN is set, so
// local builds, previews and the build before the owner creates the Cloudflare site send no analytics at all.
//
// Privacy: Cloudflare states the beacon does not store data in the browser or read cookies, localStorage or IP address, and does not
// track people across sites (developers.cloudflare.com/web-analytics, checked 2026-10-21). No consent banner is needed for it; the
// privacy page still names it. The token is a public identifier (it is visible in page source), not a secret.
//
// Snippet: the manual-embed form from Cloudflare's FAQ (type="module", token in data-cf-beacon). A module script is deferred by
// nature; `defer` is kept as well for clarity. `is:inline` stops Astro bundling the tag. The CSP allows exactly this script file and
// connect-src https://cloudflareinsights.com (src/lib/infra/headers.ts), and only when the token is configured.
// Whether a *.workers.dev hostname can be registered as a Web Analytics site is unknown (docs/m1/third-party-integration-facts.md TP-A3):
// prove it on the first preview or leave the token unset there.
const raw = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_CF_ANALYTICS_TOKEN;
const token = typeof raw === 'string' ? raw.trim() : '';
// Only plain letters and digits are accepted, so nothing can break out of the attribute.
const valid = /^[A-Za-z0-9]{16,64}$/.test(token);
---
{valid && <script is:inline type="module" defer src="https://static.cloudflareinsights.com/beacon.min.js" data-cf-beacon={JSON.stringify({ token })}></script>}
